spec/keith-everywhere/spec.kvx:14:overview = "A shared platform-contracts crate defines external principals, capability grants, action risk, approvals, audit envelopes, trace bundles, connected accounts, computer sessions, and exclusive control leases. Nine conflict-free worker streams build Meta-Harness, channel families, ACP, plugins, Composio, CUA, and teaching against that boundary while an integration owner alone edits central daemon, protocol, state, and application mounting surfaces. Meta-Harness diagnoses harness-caused failures from complete execution traces, proposes bounded shadow candidates, ranks them on a Pareto frontier, and promotes only through the existing signed self-evolution, canary, observation, and reversal path. Channel adapters normalize every platform through the durable gateway. ACP remains a client-to-agent protocol while MCP and plugins remain agent-to-tool protocols. Keith Computer is an isolated Linux workstation with semantic and visual observation, authenticated screen streaming, exclusive user-or-Keith input control, and a demonstration recorder that compiles synchronized screen, input, DOM, accessibility, and narration evidence into editable replayable TaskRecipes."
