acceptance criteria to satisfy:
  - THE diagnostic input SHALL include complete bounded execution traces, relevant harness source, task outcome, user corrections, tool schemas, context selection, retries, completion decisions, and deterministic runtime evidence.
  - FAILURES SHALL be classified as model, environment, user-input, external service, task ambiguity, or harness caused with evidence and confidence.
  - HARNESS fault categories SHALL include context selection, tool schema, tool availability, routing, planning, retry, recovery, compaction, memory selection, permission dead end, translation loss, and termination or completion logic.
  - A proposed diagnosis SHALL name the causal harness component, reproduction, expected behavioral change, target metric, baseline, threshold, cost ceiling, and revert threshold before any edit.
  - THE diagnostic agent SHALL have no ability to alter trace evidence, evaluators, hidden corpora, approval policy, protected surfaces, or promotion records.
  - A suite SHALL prove correct attribution for representative harness and non-harness failures, duplicate suppression, injection resistance, redaction, and no diagnosis from score alone when causal evidence is absent.

